    "title": "Republic Services appeals denial of Coffin Butte Landfill expansion near Corvallis - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Republic Services has appealed the Benton County Planning Commission’s decision to deny its application to expand Coffin Butte Landfill, located north of Corvallis. The Phoenix-based company also requested a 60-day extension to the Sept. 27 deadline for a final decision, which county staff granted. The new deadline is Nov. 26. The Benton County Board of Commissioners will hold a hearing on the appeal in late October. Public participation will be available remotely via Zoom, the county said in a news release. County officials did not respond to the Statesman Journal’s request for the appeal and extension documents. Coffin Butte Landfill accepts about a third of the Mid-Willamette Valley’s garbage. Marion County is its biggest customer. In July 2024, Republic Services requested a conditional use permit from the county to expand the 178-acre landfill. On July 22, 2025, the planning commission voted unanimously to deny the application , saying Republic Services had failed to prove the expansion would not seriously interfere with adjacent land uses, alter the character of the area or pose an undue burden on local services. The decision followed more than 20 hours of hearings and more than 5,000 pages of written testimony on the proposal, with the majority testifying in opposition to the expansion. Opponents raised concerns about increased traffic, noise, odors and air pollution, potential landfill fires, documented methane exceedances , recent citations for worker health and safety violations, impacts to groundwater and more. They also pointed to a U.S. Environmental Protection Agency investigation into massive methane leaks at the landfill and employee complaints about health and safety. The EPA has not finalized its investigation. The planning commission had also unanimously denied the company’s 2021 application to expand the landfill. The current application is 50% smaller than the previously proposed one. County officials said they will soon post more information about the appeal hearing, and instructions for providing written or verbal testimony, at bentoncountyor.gov/coffin-butte-landfill . Tracy Loew covers the environment at the Statesman Journal. Send comments, questions and tips: tloew@statesmanjournal.com or 503-399-6779. Follow her on X at @Tracy_Loew This article originally appeared on Salem Statesman Journal: Republic Services appeals denial of Coffin Butte Landfill expansion near Corvallis",
